      "side": 1,
      "message": "I want to understand the connection between this hook and trace_android_rvh_alloc_pages_adjust_wmark(). If after calling trace_android_rvh_alloc_pages_adjust_wmark() the system jumps to `got_pg` or `nopage` label before reaching this line, then this hook will never be called. Is that your intention? I would expect trace_android_rvh_alloc_pages_reset_wmark() to be always called once you are done with direct reclaim.\n\nAlso how is direct_reclaim_retries being used here? It seems like you are using it to adjust watermarks only on the first iteration but the places it\u0027s used seems weird.\n```\nrestart:\n...\nif (!direct_reclaim_retries)\n    trace_android_rvh_alloc_pages_adjust_wmark();\n...\nif (direct_reclaim_retries \u003c ULONG_MAX)\n\t\tdirect_reclaim_retries++;\n...\ntrace_android_rvh_alloc_pages_reset_wmark();\n...\ngoto restart;\n```\nSeems like you are adjusting the wmark only on the first iteration but you call trace_android_rvh_alloc_pages_reset_wmark() on all iterations. Also if that\u0027s the intention, direct_reclaim_retries could be just a bool and you would not need to check it against ULONG_MAX to prevent overflow.",
